.TH APFEL-TAG 1 "2026-06-02" "apfel-tag @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apfel-tag \- classify piped text into tags using Apple's on-device content-tagging model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apfel-tag
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B echo
.RI \(dq text \(dq " | " apfel-tag
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apfel-tag
reads text from standard input and classifies it into short labels using
Apple's on-device content-tagging model
.RB ( SystemLanguageModel "(useCase: .contentTagging))."
Inference runs entirely on-device on Apple Silicon Macs with Apple
Intelligence enabled. No data leaves the machine.
.PP
It is a pipe-first UNIX tool: text on standard input, tags on standard output
(one per line, or JSON).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIformat\fR
Output format:
.B plain
(one tag per line, default) or
.BR json " (" {\(dqtags\(dq:[...]} ).
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " kind"
Label category:
.BR tags " (default), " topics ", " emotions ", " actions ", or " all .
.B all
emits topics, emotions, and actions together.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-tags " n"
Cap the number of tags returned to
.IR n .
.TP
.B \-\-permissive
Relax content guardrails. Use when benign input is refused.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable colored output. Also honors
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Tags produced.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (model unavailable or refusal).
.TP
.B 2
No input piped, or invalid arguments.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any non-empty value, disables ANSI color output.
.SH EXAMPLES
echo \(dqThe headphones sound amazing.\(dq | apfel-tag
.PP
echo \(dqKubernetes pods keep crashing.\(dq | apfel-tag -o json | jq -r \(aq.tags[]\(aq
.PP
echo \(dqA thrilling, scary movie night.\(dq | apfel-tag --kind emotions
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR apfel (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Franz Enzenhofer
